<title>NETHERLANDS: AEA 1996 Far East/Australasia air cargo up 10.9pct.</title>
<headline>AEA 1996 Far East/Australasia air cargo up 10.9pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight tonne-kilometres flown by Association of European Airlines (AEA) members on Far East/Australasia routes rose by 10.9 percent in 1996 over 1995 to 9,025.06, AEA statistics show.</p>
<p>Full AEA 1996 statistics for Europe-Asia/Australasia sectors are as follows:</p>
<p>				 1996	  1995  % change 96/95</p>
<p>Freight tonne-km (m)     9,025.06    8,138.98     up 10.9</p>
<p>Freight on pax services     52.4	  53.2     down 0.8</p>
<p>Tonne-kms (m)	     17,640.0    16,119.7	 up 9.4</p>
<p>Available tonne-km (m)  24,623.4    22,347.4	up 10.2</p>
<p>Overall load factor	   71.6	  72.1     down 0.5</p>
<p>(m) = millions</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
